course: dictionary
lesson: 4853
title: The hyphen
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A hyphen (-) is a short line. It has no spaces around it, and it joins words or parts of words together, as in «well-known» or «twenty-one».
explain: The hyphen changes meaning. Read «a little-used car» and then «a little used car». With the hyphen, little-used is one idea: the car is used only a little. Without it, the words stand apart and the meaning is different.
explain: At the end of a line, a hyphen can show that a long word has been split and continues on the next line. The hyphen tells the reader that the word is not finished yet.
fact: A hyphen is short (-) and has no spaces around it.
fact: A dash is longer than a hyphen and usually has a space on each side.
fact: Hyphens join all the parts of one number: «quatre-vingt-huit» is one number, 88, not four separate numbers.
fact: «Hyphenate» is a verb. It means to join with a hyphen.
fact: From seventeen, French builds numbers with hyphens: «dix-sept» is ten-seven.
exercise: «The well-known singer arrived late.» Which word uses a hyphen to join two words? | *well-known | arrived | late | singer
exercise: What does a hyphen do at the end of a line? | Makes the word louder | Ends the sentence | *Shows that a word is split and continues on the next line | Joins two full sentences
exercise: «A little-used car» and «a little used car» mean different things. Why? | The second one has an extra word | The first one is longer | Hyphens change nothing at all | *The hyphen joins little and used into one idea
test: «Quatre-vingt-huit is one number, 88, not four separate numbers.» What does the hyphen do here? | Splits the number into four numbers | Shows a sudden break in the sentence | *Joins the parts into one number | Adds a space
test: Which mark is a dash, not a hyphen? | A tiny dot at the end of a word | A short line with no spaces, as in well-known | A small tick | *A longer mark with a space on each side
exam: What does the verb «hyphenate» mean? | To remove all punctuation | To shorten a long word | To split a sentence into two parts | *To join with a hyphen
